<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-Sept 17.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-Sept 17.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Monday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p> Rank Name		     P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1   Portman Min	    288.89   1.82</p>
<p> 2   Niugini Min	    280.58   3.90</p>
<p> 3   Mayne Nickless	 192.53   8.51</p>
<p> 4   Adel Bton Cement     123.19   1.70</p>
<p> 5   Colonial Coml	  118.58   2.17</p>
<p> 6   TNT			115.83   1.61</p>
<p> 7   Herald Rsc	     106.19   1.20</p>
<p> 8   Orion Rsc		103.49   1.78</p>
<p> 9   Forrestania Gold	84.13   2.12</p>
<p>10   Westral Forest	  70.65   1.95</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1   Dominion Min	     3.18   0.75</p>
<p> 2   Computer Power	   3.25   3.33</p>
<p> 3   Premier Inv		3.72   0.66</p>
<p> 4   Parbury Ltd		5.11   0.60</p>
<p> 5   McIntosh Sec	     6.02   0.75</p>
<p> 6   Amalgamated Hlds	 6.21   7.50</p>
